# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .env.example — Template for Environment Variables
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# HOW TO USE:
#   1. Copy this file and rename it to ".env" (remove the ".example" part)
#   2. Replace the placeholder values with your actual values
#   3. Save the file — it will be loaded automatically when the app starts
#
# IMPORTANT:
#   - Never commit your real .env file to Git (it's already in .gitignore)
#   - Never share your API key publicly
#   - The .env file must be placed in the Backend/ folder
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Google Gemini API Key (REQUIRED) ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Get your free API key at: https://aistudio.google.com/
# Click "Get API Key" → "Create API key" → Copy the key below
GOOGLE_API_KEY=your_google_api_key_here

# ── Gemini Model Name (OPTIONAL) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Which Gemini model to use for answering questions.
# Options (as of 2024):
#   gemini-1.5-flash    → Faster, cheaper, great for most use cases (DEFAULT)
#   gemini-1.5-pro      → Slower, smarter, better for complex reasoning
#   gemini-pro          → Older model, still works
# Leave this commented out to use the default (gemini-1.5-flash)
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-1.5-flash
